WEBVTT

00:00:00.353 --> 00:00:04.320
Correlation connects indicators from different public sources to understand possible

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.075
relationships.

00:00:05.075 --> 00:00:09.600
Domains, subdomains, DNS answers, certificates, internet addresses, providers,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.540
repositories, packages, websites,

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.235
and organizations can be arranged in a timeline or relationship map.

00:00:15.235 --> 00:00:16.660
Every connection should describe its evidence.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.755
A domain resolved to an address on a date.

00:00:18.755 --> 00:00:21.395
A certificate covered a hostname during a validity period.

00:00:21.395 --> 00:00:24.060
A repository referenced a domain in a file.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.180
These statements are stronger than a vague line suggesting ownership.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.760
Time prevents false relationships.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:32.925
An address can be reassigned, a certificate can expire, and a vendor can change.

00:00:32.925 --> 00:00:35.680
Place observations on a timeline before combining them.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.080
Two indicators observed years apart may not describe the same operational state.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.140
Ownership indicators include official statements, authoritative records,

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.920
consistent branding, repository control, contractual confirmation, and internal inventory.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:48.915
Each has limitations.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:53.680
Hosting, naming similarity, or one shared provider rarely proves common control.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.020
Assign confidence based on source quality, independence, consistency,

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.465
and remaining alternatives.

00:00:58.465 --> 00:01:01.800
Look for disconfirming evidence and shared-infrastructure explanations.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.975
Avoid false attribution, which can waste response effort and harm unrelated parties.

00:01:05.975 --> 00:01:09.880
A relationship map is an analytical aid, not proof by appearance.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.630
Keep source identifiers attached to nodes and edges,

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.520
distinguish observed facts from judgments,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.790
and report uncertainty so reviewers can challenge or update the model.
